<title>UK: EMU opt-outs to enjoy far less EU influence - Clarke.</title>
<headline>EMU opt-outs to enjoy far less EU influence - Clarke.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said on Wednesday that those countries unlikely to sign up for the first wave of European Economic and Monetary Union would suffer a loss of some bargaining power within the European Union.</p>
<p>&quot;The reality is that the influence at the negotiating table of those countries likely to be out (of EMU) for the foreseeable future is far, far less than the influence of the lead contenders for membership,&quot; Clarke told parliament.  </p>
<p>A first wave of European countries are scheduled to move into a single European currency on January 1, 1999.</p>
<p>-- Mike Peacock, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
